  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Change to more typical fall weather coming Friday.\n\nTemperatures warm yet again towards late summer levels, however\nsatellite clearly shows clouds moving up from the south. \n\nShowers develop this evening from south to north. A few \nthunderstorms will also be possible in Idaho and Lemhi Counties. \nFor most locations at least a tenth of an inch of rain is likely, \nin northwest MT precipitation will be showery along the front and \nthere is a 40 to 60% chance of receiving up to a tenth. After a \nfairly dry start to October, from Lost Trail Pass through \nsouthwest MT there is a 70 to 90% chance of receiving up to 1/2 of\nan inch of total precipitation by Friday evening. Above 6000 feet,\nas precipitation is ending a change over to snow is possible with\na slushy trace to 3 inches in accumulations at locations like \nGeorgetown Lake and Homestake and MacDonald Passes. Due to the \ntiming of snow around rush hour Friday evening a winter weather \nadvisory has been issued for the potential of slick driving \nconditions. \n\nThe models continue to have significant uncertainty after day 3\n(Sunday). What is clear is temperatures will catch up to the\ncalendar and October temperatures arrive. High temperatures are\nexpected to be in the 50s for western MT and 60s for north-central\nID, while low temperatures routinely fall into the teens and 20s\nin MT. Weather systems are less clear but there are more solutions\ndepicting a system by mid-week. More details to come.",
